  "lineage": "Song tradition of the Kabylie mountains of northern Algeria, moving from village achewiq women's laments and idebbalen bendir-and-ghaita processionals into the exile chanson kabyle of the Paris cafés from the 1950s, codified by Slimane Azem, Cherif Kheddam, Idir and Lounès Matoub — Tamazight-language strophic verse in Aeolian and Phrygian modes over acoustic guitar, mandole and bendir at moderate 6/8 or 2/4, with a plain unforced lead voice and unison choral refrains carrying identity politics.",
